# N3 example: unstratified-negation.
# Companion to unstratified-negation.eye/.srl: an intentional negative
# cycle (in depends on not out; out depends on not in).
#
# Unlike Eyelang and SRL, which both statically reject this rule set as
# unstratifiable, N3 has no stratification analysis at all -- its
# negation-as-failure (log:notIncludes) is instead handled by an ad hoc
# "defer until the ordinary closure saturates, then resume" mechanism.
# For a genuine cycle like this one, that mechanism does not detect the
# problem; it just settles on whichever side's check happens to resolve
# first (here, :In), an implementation-order-dependent result rather than
# a principled rejection or a properly stratified answer.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/unstratified-negation#>.

:alice a :Person.

{?x a :Person. ?SCOPE log:notIncludes {?x a :Out}.} => {?x a :In}.
{?x a :Person. ?SCOPE log:notIncludes {?x a :In}.} => {?x a :Out}.
